        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>The End of the End - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/the-end-of-the-end/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"The End of the End - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Pepuza. That’s not a name that probably means anything to modern ears. In the late the second century, a radical self-proclaimed prophet named Montanus declared that Pepuza—a remote village in Phrygia (modern date Turkey)—would be the location of the second coming. &nbsp; His prophecies were accompanied by ecstatic experiences and strange utterances, thought by his [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/the-end-of-the-end/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-09-21T13:50:06+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-09-21T15:48:26+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/End-of-End-scaled.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1920\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"2560\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />\n<script type=\"application/ld+js