        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>A New Academic Volume on the Origins of the New Testament Canon - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/a-new-academic-volume-on-the-origins-of-the-new-testament-canon/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"A New Academic Volume on the Origins of the New Testament Canon - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"It goes without saying that not all academic sub-disciplines (especially in the field of biblical studies) generate the same level of scholarly interest. Some fields are more active; others less so. And it can change from generation to generation. When I was doing my work with Larry Hurtado years ago at the University of Edinburgh, [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/a-new-academic-volume-on-the-origins-of-the-new-testament-canon/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-05-01T15:18:25+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-09-14T14:16:41+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/nt-canon-contemporary.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"897\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"537\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta