        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>Does the World Notice When Christians Fight with One Another? - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://canonfodder.wpenginepowered.com/does-the-world-notice-when-christians-fight-with-one-another/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Does the World Notice When Christians Fight with One Another? - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"In the earliest centuries of the church, the burgeoning Christian movement had its fair share of critics. And their complaints were wide and varied. Christians worshipped a criminal crucified by the Romans. Christians were a threat to the empire because of their refusal to pay homage to the gods. Christian books were filled with errors [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://canonfodder.wpenginepowered.com/does-the-world-notice-when-christians-fight-with-one-another/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-03-02T14:46:25+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-03-02T14:52:57+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2026/02/fighting.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"2219\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"1982\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=