    {
      "source": "kruger",
      "sourceId": "16269",
      "title": "What is the Real Meaning of Christmas? A Wonderful New Kids Book Provides the Answer!",
      "author": "Michael Kruger",
      "url": "https://michaeljkruger.com/what-is-the-real-meaning-of-christmas-a-wonderful-new-kids-book-provides-the-answer/",
      "sha256": "7a033507bb6eba17bebcad37df02ddce550d81edd1f8a82fbda80ab9fc79ee15",
      "bytes": 7481,
      "format": "html",
      "path": "D:\\FortressOfSolitude\\Jarvis\\Projects\\BibleProject\\sources\\library\\bulk\\kruger\\16269.html",
      "acquiredAt": "2026-10-07T20:12:44.166706+00:00",
      "language": "en",
      "audience": "adult readers; pastors; scholars",
      "campaignMission": "RB08",
      "licence": "Copyright retained by author/ministry; publicly offered written material; private local research copy; original notices and credits retained",
      "useScope": "private local import and embedding",
      "contributor": "Michael Kruger",
      "credit": "kruger",
      "sourceApi": "https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?per_page=100&page=1",
      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 16269,
        "date": "2025-12-01T10:45:15",
        "date_gmt": "2025-12-01T15:45:15",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "https://michaeljkruger.com/?p=16269"
        },
        "modified": "2025-12-01T10:45:15",
        "modified_gmt": "2025-12-01T15:45:15",
        "slug": "what-is-the-real-meaning-of-christmas-a-wonderful-new-kids-book-provides-the-answer",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/what-is-the-real-meaning-of-christmas-a-wonderful-new-kids-book-provides-the-answer/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "What is the Real Meaning of Christmas? A Wonderful New Kids Book Provides the Answer!"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>What is the real meaning of Christmas?  During this festive time of the year, many are busy reminding us that the meaning certainly has nothing to do with presents.  Let’s not buy into the materialistic side of Christmas, we are told.  Let’s not focus on the gifts.</p>\n<p>Now let me say that the sentiment behind such concerns is entirely valid.  Few would disagree with the fact that Christmas (especially in America) is overly commercialized and materialistic.  And certainly we would want to resist this trend as much as possible.</p>\n<p>However, is the denigration of gifts really the way to accomplish this?  Are gifts the problem?  Not necessarily.  Year ago, <a href=\"https://melissabkruger.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">my wife Melissa</a> wrote an article my wife wrote on this topic for the <a href=\"http://thegospelcoalition.org/blogs/tgc/2012/12/17/the-season-of-giving/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gospel Coalition</a>.  She provides a healthy balance by reminding us that while giving gifts can be distorted by our sinful natures, it can also reflect the gift-giving God we serve and in whose image we are made.  Here is an excerpt:</p>\n<blockquote><p><em>As I discussed my internal struggle with my husband, he kindly reminded me that gift giving does not so much reflect worldly materialism as our Creator, who delights to give gifts to his people. I bear within my humanity the stamp of his image. There is something of the divine nature in yearning to give to others.</em></p>\n<p><em>He also reminded me that while we bear the image of our Creator, it is marred and broken by the Fall. A good desire becomes twisted and results in sin. Rather than glorify the Creator, gift giving is often rooted in the desire for self-glory. My internal wrestling exhibits the war between what I was created to be and the effects of sin.</em></p>\n<p><em>Our car ride conversation prompted me to ponder anew the glory of the gift that God freely gave on that night in Bethlehem. These reflections have filled my heart with a deep joy and thanksgiving. Reveling in the wonder of the true and lovely fills the shadows of earthly gift giving with substance.</em></p>\n<p><em>Truly special gifts usually involve preparation and waiting. From the exit of Eden, a promise of redemption and a hope was given. The divine whisper continued speaking through all the prophets: Something special is coming. Wait for it. Watch for it. Hope in it.</em></p>\n<p><em>And then, at just the right moment in time, God sent angels and a star in the heavens to declare, “The gift is here.” Glory wrapped in flesh made his dwelling among us in the form of a baby. It was unexpected. It was surprising. It was exactly what we needed.</em></p></blockquote>\n<p>It was this very discussion—and the realization of the importance of gifts at Christmas reflecting God&#8217;s gift in Christ—that has led Melissa to write her most recent kids books. It&#8217;s entitled, <a href=\"https://amzn.to/4onjGMp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>The Gift of All Gifts</em></a>, and it is really wonderful. Filled with catchy rhymes and engaging illustrations, this book reminds kids (and all of us), that Christ is truly the gift of all gifts.</p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s an excerpt:<a href=\"https://amzn.to/3M8UnAm\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"16271\" data-permalink=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/what-is-the-real-meaning-of-christmas-a-wonderful-new-kids-book-provides-the-answer/giftofgifts/\" data-orig-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1037,1280\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"giftofgifts\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts-1024x1264.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-16271\" src=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"507\" height=\"625\" srcset=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts.jpg 1037w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts-400x494.jpg 400w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts-1024x1264.jpg 1024w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/12/giftofgifts-768x948.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 507px) 100vw, 507px\" /></a></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\"><em>I see you peeking,</em><br />\n<em>Searching to find</em><br />\n<em>Something that&#8217;s yours</em><br />\n<em>Something that shines.</em></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\"><em>What are you hoping for</em><br />\n<em>Under the tree? </em><br />\n<em>What are you dreaming</em><br />\n<em>That present might be? </em></p>\n<p>And here are the endorsements:</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">A cozy Christmas read with Christ at the center, this book has a timeless message with a nostalgic aesthetic. Many families will enjoy this together!&#8221;<br />\n&#8211;Emily A. Jensen, cofounder of Risen Motherhood</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;I want to give The Gift of All Gifts to everyone because it points us to Jesus&#8211;the greatest gift of all. Using rhythm and rhyme, Kruger winsomely reminds us of the true meaning of Christmas. What a gift!&#8221; &#8211;Hunter Beless, author and founder of Journeywomen Ministries</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;The children&#8217;s books by Melissa Kruger always stick with me and my family. She has a special gift for writing eternal truth in memorable ways for all ages. I&#8217;m excited to add this book to my family&#8217;s Christmas rotation.&#8221;<br />\n&#8211;Collin Hansen, vice president for content and editor in chief for The Gospel Coalition</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;Why do we give and receive gifts at Christmas? For families with young kids, this question is a natural entry point to a Christmas-season gospel conversation&#8211;and The Gift of All Gifts is a great facilitator for that discussion. Beautifully illustrated and delightfully written, this will be a new staple for me to read with my kids each December!&#8221;<br />\n&#8211;Brett McCracken, senior editor at The Gospel Coalition and author of The Wisdom Pyramid</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;Melissa Kruger writes some of my favorite children&#8217;s books, and The Gift of All Gifts is no different. The fun, catchy rhymes, repeated phrases, cozy illustrations, and important message will make this a book your family pulls out year after year.&#8221;<br />\n&#8211;Laura Wifler, cofounder of Risen Motherhood and bestselling author of Any Time, Any Place, Any Prayer</p>\n<p>If you&#8217;re looking for a present for your kids (or grandkids) at Christmas, this book would be perfect. You can check it out <a href=\"https://amzn.to/4onjGMp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>!</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
