        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>Sleeping with the Gospels - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://canonfodder.wpenginepowered.com/sleeping-with-the-gospels/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Sleeping with the Gospels - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Not many Christians carry around Bibles anymore these days. In my younger years, I can remember that it was standard fare to carry your Bible to church. Even in college, we would take our Bibles to the evening gathering of our campus fellowship. To have a worn, tattered Bible—due to regularly carrying it around in [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://canonfodder.wpenginepowered.com/sleeping-with-the-gospels/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2025-02-18T16:10:24+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2025-04-04T19:47:37+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2025/02/Sleeping-with-Gospels-scaled.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"2560\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"1966\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"6 minutes\" />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json