        "slug": "frank-turek-on-predestination-a-roman-critique-of-eoism-as-petrified-and-andrew-isker-on-supporting-the-murder-of-fritz-erbe-and-others",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://www.aomin.org/aoblog/the-dividing-line/frank-turek-on-predestination-a-roman-critique-of-eoism-as-petrified-and-andrew-isker-on-supporting-the-murder-of-fritz-erbe-and-others/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Frank Turek on Predestination, a Roman Critique of EOism as &#8220;Petrified,&#8221; and Andrew Isker on Supporting the Murder of Fritz Erbe (and others)"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Played a clip where Dr. Turek uses a form of Molinism to respond to a question on predestination.  Before or after that (funny how it is hard to remember right after doing the show!) we looked at a graphic where a Roman Catholic says the Orthodox are &#8220;Petrified&#8221; as in fossilized in time, and what that might mean.  Then we spent the rest of the time looking at my exchange with Andrew Isker on the imprisonment and eventual death of Fritz Erbe and others in the sacral period after the Reformation.  A useful exposure of where Isker, and those allied with him, are really going. And again, for those interested in the story of what happened at Münster, here are the two programs I did on Sheologians:  <a href=\"https://sheologians.com/storytime-with-dr-james-white-the-blood-streets-of-muenster-part-1/\">here</a> and <a href=\"https://sheologians.com/story-time-w-dr-james-white-the-bloody-streets-of-muenster-part-2/\">here</a>. </p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/69251543464003/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Frank Turek on Predestination, a Roman Critique of EOism &quot;Petrified,&quot; &amp; Andrew Isker on Fritz Erbe\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/k_dy1yZIEtw?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Played a clip where Dr. Turek uses a form of Molinism to respond to a question on predestination. Before or after that (funny how it is hard to remember right after doing the show!) we looked at a graphic where a Roman Catholic says the Orthodox are &#8220;Petrified&#8221; as in fossilized in time, and what that might mean. Then we [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
