        "title": {
          "rendered": "Jay Dyer Implodes on the Playground; Yes, Joe, Bishop and Elder are the Same Office"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">About halfway through the program we had a power spike due to a storm blowing into Phoenix, but we got it all recorded anyway.  First I dealt with the amazing explosion of infantile behavior by one Jay Dyer when I dared actually treat him like an adult in challenging him to defend Nicea II in debate.  You won&#8217;t believe his behavior.  Then we transitioned into an examination of the reality, acknowledged by all, really, that &#8220;presbuteros&#8221; and &#8220;episkopos&#8221; in the Greek New Testament refer to the very same office, a reality disputed by Joe Heschmeyer in our debate in Jonesboro.  Enjoy!</p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/314250253429/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Jay Dyer Implodes on the Playground; Yes, Joe, Bishop and Elder are the Same Office\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/gXK1inG8pDI?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>About halfway through the program we had a power spike due to a storm blowing into Phoenix, but we got it all recorded anyway. First I dealt with the amazing explosion of infantile behavior by one Jay Dyer when I dared actually treat him like an adult in challenging him to defend Nicea II in debate. You won&#8217;t believe his [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
