        "title": {
          "rendered": "Live Feed Link to White/Horn Sola Scriptura Debate"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Calvinist James White and Roman Catholic Trent Horn will debate the &#8220;formal principle&#8221; of the Reformation, sola scriptura, or Scripture Alone. From Luther on, Protestants have argued that the Bible is the only &#8220;God-breathed&#8221; revelation that can provide sufficient knowledge of God and His salvation. Roman Catholics argue that the Tradition is equally valid and important as a source. The disagreement on sources has led to a host of other disagreements. Who is right? Both speakers are the top apologists in their fields, so this debate promises to be both interesting and important.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"White/Horn Sola Scriptura Debate\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CV01DNwNmig?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Calvinist James White and Roman Catholic Trent Horn will debate the &#8220;formal principle&#8221; of the Reformation, sola scriptura, or Scripture Alone. From Luther on, Protestants have argued that the Bible is the only &#8220;God-breathed&#8221; revelation that can provide sufficient knowledge of God and His salvation. Roman Catholics argue that the Tradition is equally valid and important as a source. The [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
