        "title": {
          "rendered": "Happenings in Rome, Acts 15, and Provisionist Rhetoric"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Started off with more on the continuing developments with Francis, Fernandez, and the Roman Church, moving sort of seamlessly into @ReformedtoRome&#8217;s attempt to use Acts 15 as a defeater of <em>sola scriptura</em>.  Then we looked at some recent @Soteriology101 statements on the idea of being made &#8220;better&#8221; so as to believe in Calvinism.</p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/192420217268/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Happenings in Rome, Acts 15, and Provisionist Rhetoric\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ht49ctjUawY?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Started off with more on the continuing developments with Francis, Fernandez, and the Roman Church, moving sort of seamlessly into @ReformedtoRome&#8217;s attempt to use Acts 15 as a defeater of sola scriptura. Then we looked at some recent @Soteriology101 statements on the idea of being made &#8220;better&#8221; so as to believe in Calvinism.</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
