        "title": {
          "rendered": "How Did We Get Our Bible? My Interview on the NT Canon at the Ligonier Conference"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>This past March I spoke at the <a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/learn/conferences/upholding-christian-ethics-2022-national-conference/the-truth-about-marriage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ligonier National Conference</a>. My plenary address was on &#8220;The Truth about Marriage&#8221; (you can watch <a href=\"https://youtu.be/XVSJXoPHb6A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>), and I also did an enjoyable sit-down interview on the subject of the origins of the New Testament canon. You can watch below!</p>\n<p>[iframe width=&#8221;600&#8243; height=&#8221;400&#8243; src=&#8221;https://www.youtube.com/embed/DTki0ESXIJk&#8221; title=&#8221;YouTube video player&#8221; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allow=&#8221;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#8221; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>This past March I spoke at the Ligonier National Conference. My plenary address was on &#8220;The Truth about Marriage&#8221; (you can watch here), and I also did an enjoyable sit-down interview on the subject of the origins of the New Testament canon. You can watch below! [iframe width=&#8221;600&#8243; height=&#8221;400&#8243; src=&#8221;https://www.youtube.com/embed/DTki0ESXIJk&#8221; title=&#8221;YouTube video player&#8221; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allow=&#8221;accelerometer; [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
