        "title": {
          "rendered": "Rutgers&#8217; Racist Professor, More Muhammed Hijab, and the Neo-Socinian Nonsense Again"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Back in Phoenix in our regular studio, so we looked briefly at the racist Rutgers professor and &#8220;white folks,&#8221; then we spent about twenty minutes responding to more of Muhammed Hijab&#8217;s opening statement against the Trinity, and then listened to a few minutes of the &#8220;Coffee House Sessions&#8221; webcast on the modern state of Reformed Baptist and Robert Briggs&#8217; accusation that biblicism is neo-Socinianism and that this is the reason for the division amongst real, confessional Reformed Baptists and those who just &#8220;pretend.&#8221; Sad days for the RB movement, to be sure.</p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/121423162285064/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Rutgers&#039; Racist Professor, More Muhammed Hijab, and the Neo-Socinian Nonsense Again\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/R2Z5ASK1GNg?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Back in Phoenix in our regular studio, so we looked briefly at the racist Rutgers professor and &#8220;white folks,&#8221; then we spent about twenty minutes responding to more of Muhammed Hijab&#8217;s opening statement against the Trinity, and then listened to a few minutes of the &#8220;Coffee House Sessions&#8221; webcast on the modern state of Reformed Baptist and Robert Briggs&#8217; accusation [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
