      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 9552,
        "date": "2022-02-17T09:39:15",
        "date_gmt": "2022-02-17T14:39:15",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=9552"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T18:02:16",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T22:02:16",
        "slug": "my-six-part-ligonier-video-series-on-the-new-testament-canon",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/my-six-part-ligonier-video-series-on-the-new-testament-canon/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "My Six-Part @Ligonier Video Series on The New Testament Canon"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>Since next month I will be speaking at the <a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/events/2022-national-conference/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ligonier National Conference</a> in Orlando, FL, I thought I might highlight a video series I did for Ligonier a few years ago. It is a six-part video series (available <a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/store/the-new-testament-canon-dvd/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> in either digital or DVD format) on the origins, authority, and development of the NT Canon.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/store/the-new-testament-canon-dvd/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"7338\" data-permalink=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/its-here-my-new-ligonier-dvd-series-on-the-origins-of-the-nt-canon/nt-canon-ligonier/\" data-orig-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"200,280\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"NT-Canon-Ligonier\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-7338 \" src=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"237\" height=\"332\" /></a></p>\n<p>One of the most common questions I am asked is whether I have introductory, lay-level material on the origins of the NT canon that people can use in their churches.  For small group Bible studies or Sunday School classes, most people simply won’t read <a href=\"https://amzn.to/2Ue8NhN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Canon Revisited</em></a> or any of my <a href=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">other books</a>.</p>\n<p>So, my hope is that this video series will meet a need for churches looking to do something on the canon but not knowing where to turn.</p>\n<p>If you want an overview, here is a short video where I introduce the series and provide a quick summary of why we can trust the NT canon:<!--more--><span id=\"more-7335\"></span></p>\n<p>[iframe width=&#8221;600&#8243; height=&#8221;338&#8243; src=&#8221;https://www.youtube.com/embed/ucfrxLOnl4k&#8221; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allow=&#8221;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#8221; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Since next month I will be speaking at the Ligonier National Conference in Orlando, FL, I thought I might highlight a video series I did for Ligonier a few years ago. It is a six-part video series (available here in either digital or DVD format) on the origins, authority, and development of the NT Canon. [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
