          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=9322"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T18:02:26",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T22:02:26",
        "slug": "check-out-the-rtscharlotte-womens-bible-study-on-the-book-of-hebrews",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/check-out-the-rtscharlotte-womens-bible-study-on-the-book-of-hebrews/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Check Out the @RTSCharlotte Women&#8217;s Bible Study on the Book of Hebrews"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>Back in 2017-2019, I taught a weekly Bible study for women on the <a href=\"https://rts.edu/campuses/charlotte/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RTS Charlotte campus</a>. For 33 weeks, about 150 women gathered together to study the book of Hebrews in all its richness and depth.</p>\n<p>Thankfully, our great video team here, led by Matt McQuade, captured that series in HD video.  We have made the <a href=\"https://rts.edu/hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">entire Bible study</a> available to the public for free, <a href=\"https://rts.edu/hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">including handouts</a> for each installment.</p>\n<p>Since their release, we have been so encouraged to see how these videos have been utilized by groups all over the country and the world. I have received emails from places like Slovakia and Indonesia, telling us that they have used these videos for their Bible study groups.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://amzn.to/39pC43b\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"9324\" data-permalink=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/check-out-the-rtscharlotte-womens-bible-study-on-the-book-of-hebrews/hebrewsforyou/\" data-orig-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1594,2539\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Hebrewsforyou\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-1024x1631.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-9324\" src=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-400x637.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"155\" height=\"247\" srcset=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-400x637.jpg 400w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-1024x1631.jpg 1024w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-768x1223.jpg 768w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-964x1536.jpg 964w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou-1286x2048.jpg 1286w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2021/09/Hebrewsforyou.jpg 1594w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 155px) 100vw, 155px\" /></a>If you are leading a Bible study and looking for good content, we hope you will check out the series. Also, this past year I released my new commentary on the book of Hebrews, entitled <a href=\"https://amzn.to/39pC43b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Hebrews For You</em></a> (Good Book Company, 2020), which was developed out of the material for the class.</p>\n<p>If you are interested in learning more, check out the videos <a href=\"https://rts.edu/hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>!</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Back in 2017-2019, I taught a weekly Bible study for women on the RTS Charlotte campus. For 33 weeks, about 150 women gathered together to study the book of Hebrews in all its richness and depth. Thankfully, our great video team here, led by Matt McQuade, captured that series in HD video.  We have made [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
