          "og_type": "article",
          "og_title": "One of the Earliest (and Clearest) Summaries of Early Christian Beliefs - Canon Fodder",
          "og_description": "A common claim among critics of Christianity is that early Christian doctrine was a bit of a mess. What we believe now—about the incarnation, divinity of Jesus, etc.—was a late development within the early Christian movement. And, so the implication goes, the earliest Christians did not necessarily believe the same things as later Christians. Now, [&hellip;]",
          "og_url": "https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/one-of-the-earliest-and-clearest-summaries-of-early-christian-beliefs/",
