        "title": {
          "rendered": "Open Phones on the Dividing Line"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Started off showing my newly &#8220;dyed&#8221; Bible texts, following the process laid out by Jeffery Rice in <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Bh_It8tbVPM\">this video</a>, and then took calls on Rushdooney, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/b_QkvpIcdUc\">Alma Allred</a> (Mormonism), recognizing novel and soon to be abandoned ideas in theology, wokeness in the Assemblies of God, and dealing with Jehovah&#8217;s Witnesses on the eternality of Jesus.  Also, we had one Modalistic caller who tried to say Martin Luther denied the Trinity.  <a href=\"https://beggarsallreformation.blogspot.com/2010/01/luther-condemned-word-trinity.html\">Here is an article</a> debunking that mythology. </p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/811232231255353/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"Open Phones on the Dividing Line\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/9x40duzRW-g?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Started off showing my newly &#8220;dyed&#8221; Bible texts, following the process laid out by Jeffery Rice in this video, and then took calls on Rushdooney, Alma Allred (Mormonism), recognizing novel and soon to be abandoned ideas in theology, wokeness in the Assemblies of God, and dealing with Jehovah&#8217;s Witnesses on the eternality of Jesus. Also, we had one Modalistic caller [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
