        "title": {
          "rendered": "A New Low of Depravity, Wolfe on Dever, Anthony Bernabei Exposed"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Managed a solid live stream today, thankfully! Started off with an amazing example of &#8220;no, we haven&#8217;t hit rock bottom quite yet, but man we are digging hard&#8221; as far as the evil of man is concerned.  Then we looked at Stephen Wolfe&#8217;s comments in response to Mark Dever on paedobaptism and a regenerate church membership. Finished up looking at the rhetoric of one Anthony Bernabei, a wild-eyed unitarian whose immaturity precludes him from serious consideration, but yet he provided a useful example of unitarian deception that allowed us to dig deeply into John 17 and 1 Corinthians 8.  75 minutes today!</p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/71323222937139/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"A New Low of Depravity, Wolfe on Dever, Anthony Bernabei Exposed\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/3mZSuJx9ZXc?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Managed a solid live stream today, thankfully! Started off with an amazing example of &#8220;no, we haven&#8217;t hit rock bottom quite yet, but man we are digging hard&#8221; as far as the evil of man is concerned. Then we looked at Stephen Wolfe&#8217;s comments in response to Mark Dever on paedobaptism and a regenerate church membership. Finished up looking at [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
