          "rendered": "Thinking Through the Ugandan Controversy"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is very sad that the the Church does not speak with a unified voice in the modern world. Yet it remains our duty to think through, as Christians, the key issues we are facing in this world gone insane with its destructive rebellion.  Today we looked at the comparison of a progressivist, &#8220;liberal&#8221; view on homosexuality with the comments of Russell Moore on the Ugandan law prohibiting homosexuality. Also, discovered that a playlist has been posted on YouTube for the Holiness Code series (38 sermons), which you can find <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLzOwqed_gET38HNI6V5U5k9NlKaHBfnZs\">here</a>.  </p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/61232040237370/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n",
          "protected": false
        },
