        "title": {
          "rendered": "A Few Reflections on Forty Years, John Pavlovitz and the Sin of Homophobia"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I was Chris Arnzen&#8217;s guest on <a href=\"https://www.ironsharpensironradio.com/\">Iron Sharpens Iron</a> today, and then 15 minutes later we did the Dividing Line.  I am in Tucumcari, New Mexico, making my way home in the mobile command center, truly enjoying our new studio, Starlink web access, etc.  Despite some pretty strong thunderstorms we maintained connection and discussed forty years of ministry in the first half hour before looking at an article by &#8220;progressivist&#8221; <a href=\"https://johnpavlovitz.com/2023/03/03/an-open-apology-to-homophobic-and-transphobic-christians/\">John Pavlovitz</a> on the sin of Christian homophobia.  Talked a bit about how we can use the coming Month of Debauchery to press forward the claims of King Jesus.</p>\n\n\n\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://embed.sermonaudio.com/player/a/523232152306189/\" style=\"min-width: 150px;\" scrolling=\"no\" width=\"100%\" height=\"150\" frameborder=\"0\"></iframe>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"A Few Reflections on Forty Years, John Pavlovitz and the Sin of Homophobia\" width=\"1200\" height=\"675\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/V0N5c_spJl4?feature=oembed&amp;wmode=opaque&amp;showinfo=0\" style=\"border: none\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>I was Chris Arnzen&#8217;s guest on Iron Sharpens Iron today, and then 15 minutes later we did the Dividing Line. I am in Tucumcari, New Mexico, making my way home in the mobile command center, truly enjoying our new studio, Starlink web access, etc. Despite some pretty strong thunderstorms we maintained connection and discussed forty years of ministry in the [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
