      "credit": "kruger",
      "sourceApi": "https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?per_page=100&page=4",
      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 8827,
        "date": "2021-02-25T08:18:34",
        "date_gmt": "2021-02-25T13:18:34",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=8827"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T18:00:42",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T22:00:42",
        "slug": "what-do-we-do-when-our-view-of-morality-is-seen-as-hateful-and-intolerant",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/what-do-we-do-when-our-view-of-morality-is-seen-as-hateful-and-intolerant/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "What Do We Do When Our View of Morality Is Seen as Hateful and Intolerant?"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>I am working my way through <a href=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/how-i-almost-lost-my-faith-in-college-a-preview-of-my-latest-book/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">a blog series</a> in anticipation of my forthcoming book, <a href=\"https://amzn.to/35B6jCV\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Surviving Religion 101: Letters to a Christian Student on Keeping the Faith in College</em> </a>(Crossway, 2021). This new series will include 7 videos that tackle key intellectual questions about the Christian faith.</p>\n<p>This fifth video deals with one of the most common challenges we face: &#8220;My Views Are Seen as Hateful and Intolerant: Should I Change Them?&#8221;</p>\n<p>Here we come to the issue of the Christian view of <em>morality</em>. For those on a secular college campus, there&#8217;s nothing that makes you feel out of place more quickly than your distinctive moral code.</p>\n<p class=\"Normal\">Of course, college campuses have never been known as bastions of moral virtue. The party atmosphere and near-hedonistic tendencies of modern university life are well known (as captured in all the 1980s movies I watched growing up). Even so, something has shifted—and shifted dramatically—in the last generation. And this shift is most evident in the way people approach the issue of sex and sexuality.</p>\n<p>No longer is sex just something people <span class=\"Italic\">do</span>, it is viewed as core to who they <span class=\"Italic\">are</span>. People have attached their “identity” to their sexual activity and their sexual preferences. The two—sex and identity—are now inextricably intertwined.</p>\n<p class=\"Normal\">This means that Christian views on morality—especially as they pertain to sex—will be seen as a personal attack on people. While in prior generations the biblical view of sex would have just been viewed as old-fashioned and stodgy, now it is viewed as downright hateful and discriminatory. It’s regarded not as just a different opinion but as a full-frontal assault on another person’s dignity and worth.</p>\n<p class=\"Normal\">In other words, much of the world considers the Christian view of sex—more to the point, the Bible’s view of sex—as <span class=\"Italic\">immoral</span>. (Just let the irony of that sink in for a moment).</p>\n<p class=\"Normal\">And here’s what’s going to happen (and probably already has happened). You will begin to doubt the goodness and rightness of your moral positions. You may wonder if <em><span class=\"Italic\">you</span> </em>are the problem. You may begin to feel like you’re a hateful, discriminatory person. And this might tempt you to change your views so that you are seen as more “loving” and “tolerant.”</p>\n<p>So, how do we respond to this challenge?  Here&#8217;s my latest video:<!--more--></p>\n<p>[iframe title=&#8221;vimeo-player&#8221; src=&#8221;https://player.vimeo.com/video/467430357&#8243; width=&#8221;640&#8243; height=&#8221;360&#8243; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>I am working my way through a blog series in anticipation of my forthcoming book, Surviving Religion 101: Letters to a Christian Student on Keeping the Faith in College (Crossway, 2021). This new series will include 7 videos that tackle key intellectual questions about the Christian faith. This fifth video deals with one of the [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
