      "useScope": "private local import and embedding",
      "contributor": "Michael Kruger",
      "credit": "kruger",
      "sourceApi": "https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?per_page=100&page=4",
      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 8448,
        "date": "2020-10-13T10:04:28",
        "date_gmt": "2020-10-13T14:04:28",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=8448"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T17:59:53",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T21:59:53",
        "slug": "looking-for-a-lay-level-class-on-the-origins-of-the-nt-canon-heres-my-6-part-video-series-with-ligonier",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/looking-for-a-lay-level-class-on-the-origins-of-the-nt-canon-heres-my-6-part-video-series-with-ligonier/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Looking for a Lay-Level Class on the Origins of the NT Canon? Here&#8217;s my 6-Part Video Series with @Ligonier"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>One of the most common questions I am asked is whether I have introductory, lay-level material on the origins of the NT canon that people can use in their churches.  For small group Bible studies or Sunday School classes, most people simply won’t read <a href=\"https://amzn.to/2Ue8NhN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Canon Revisited</em></a> or any of my <a href=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">other books</a>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/store/the-new-testament-canon-dvd/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"7338\" data-permalink=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/its-here-my-new-ligonier-dvd-series-on-the-origins-of-the-nt-canon/nt-canon-ligonier/\" data-orig-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"200,280\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"NT-Canon-Ligonier\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-7338 size-full\" src=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/NT-Canon-Ligonier.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"280\" /></a>So, I point the reader to my recent video series with <a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/store/the-new-testament-canon-dvd/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ligonier</a> where I give six introductory lectures on the origins and authority of the NT canon.  My hope is that this will meet a need for churches looking to do something on canon but not knowing where to turn.</p>\n<p>You can order the videos <a href=\"https://www.ligonier.org/store/the-new-testament-canon-dvd/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> in either digital or DVD format. Here is a short video where I introduce the series and provide a quick summary of why we can trust the NT canon:<!--more--><span id=\"more-7335\"></span></p>\n<p>[iframe width=&#8221;600&#8243; height=&#8221;338&#8243; src=&#8221;https://www.youtube.com/embed/ucfrxLOnl4k&#8221; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allow=&#8221;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#8221; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>One of the most common questions I am asked is whether I have introductory, lay-level material on the origins of the NT canon that people can use in their churches.  For small group Bible studies or Sunday School classes, most people simply won’t read Canon Revisited or any of my other books. So, I point [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "author": 2,
        "featured_media": 8452,
        "comment_status": "open",
