        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>How Early Christianity was Mocked for Welcoming Women - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"How Early Christianity was Mocked for Welcoming Women - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"I recently received a question on Twitter about where in our patristic sources we see early Christianity mocked for being a religion filled with women.  The short answer: lots of places. But before we get there, we should begin by noting that early Christianity received this criticism precisely because it was so popular with women [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2020-07-13T13:53:28+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2023-04-14T21:59:59+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2020/07/women-e1594648356940.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1000\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"498\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"4 minutes\" />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"Michael Kruger\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/b985803864f1d81b09c01a0aa8aa6d22\"},\"headline\":\"How Early Christianity was Mocked for Welcoming Women\",\"datePublished\":\"2020-07-13T13:53:28+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2023-04-14T21:59:59+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/\"},\"wordCount\":835,\"commentCount\":24,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/b985803864f1d81b09c01a0aa8aa6d22\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/5mt.michaeljkruger.com\\/2020\\/07\\/women-e1594648356940.jpg\",\"keywords\":[\"role of women\",\"women in early Christianity\",\"women in the early church\"],\"articleSection\":[\"Culture &amp; Politics\",\"Women's Ministry\"],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"CommentAction\",\"name\":\"Comment\",\"target\":[\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/#respond\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/how-early-christianity-was-mocked-for-welcoming-women\\/\",\"name\":\"How Early Christianity was Mocked for Welcoming Women - Canon Fodder\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\"