          "og_title": "How a \"You do You\" Culture Has Made Us Vulnerable to the Coronavirus - Canon Fodder",
          "og_description": "&#8220;You do you.&#8221; Perhaps there&#8217;s no phrase that captures our current cultural moment better. Back in 2015, Colson Whitehead of the New York Times Magazine, lamented this phrase, arguing that it &#8220;perfectly captures our narcissistic culture.&#8221; Indeed, it is hard to disagree. &#8220;You do you&#8221; embodies our culture&#8217;s commitment to personal fulfillment, self-actualization, and the [&hellip;]",
