      "useScope": "private local import and embedding",
      "contributor": "Michael Kruger",
      "credit": "kruger",
      "sourceApi": "https://michaeljkruger.com/wp-json/wp/v2/posts?per_page=100&page=4",
      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 7681,
        "date": "2019-11-15T09:18:19",
        "date_gmt": "2019-11-15T14:18:19",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=7681"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T17:59:18",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T21:59:18",
        "slug": "off-to-san-diego-for-the-annual-meeting-of-the-evangelical-theological-society",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/off-to-san-diego-for-the-annual-meeting-of-the-evangelical-theological-society/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Off to San Diego for the Annual Meeting of the Evangelical Theological Society"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>Next week, I head to beautiful San Diego for the 71st Annual Meeting of the <a href=\"https://www.etsjets.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Evangelical Theological Society</em></a>, the largest gathering of evangelical scholars in the world. The theme this year is &#8220;Christ in All Scripture.&#8221;</p>\n<p>This year I will be delivering the presidential address at the Thursday night banquet. The title of my lecture is &#8220;2 Peter 3:2, the Apostolate and a Bi-Covenantal Canon.&#8221;  Yes, I know. Not that exciting. But, that&#8217;s just what we scholars do&#8230;</p>\n<p>For more exciting lectures, you may want to check out the three plenary speakers we have lined up:  Greg Beale (Westminster Seminary), Jeannine Brown (Bethel Seminary), and Stephen Wellum (Southern Baptist Seminary).  I thankful for my friend and program chair, Craig Keener, for lining up these three wonderful scholars.</p>\n<p>I will also be moderating the invited sessions of the study group I co-chair, &#8220;NT Canon, Textual Criticism, and Apocryphal Literature.&#8221; It meets 3-6PM, Thursday, Nov 21, Third Floor, Mission Beach BC.  We have wonderful papers from Dirk Jongkind, Elijah Hixson, and Chuck Hill. (Stan Porter was set to give a paper but was unable to make it).</p>\n<p>The open session of the NT canon group meets 8:30-11:40AM, on that same day and in the same location. Chuck Hill is moderating, and we have some great papers by Chris Stevens, Sylvie Raquel, Benjamin Laird, and John J.H. Lee.</p>\n<p>It is also worth nothing that a number of <a href=\"https://rts.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RTS</a> profs are giving papers, including Chuck Hill, Nick Reid, Dick Belcher, Blair Smith, Ben Gladd, Miles Van Pelt, John Fesko, and Michael Allen (I am sure I left some names out). There are also many RTS profs attending who are not giving papers (some are moderating sessions).</p>\n<p>Aside from all the fine papers being given, I look forward most to catching up with colleagues and friends, especially those I only see once a year at conferences like this. If you are going, I hope to see you there!</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Next week, I head to beautiful San Diego for the 71st Annual Meeting of the Evangelical Theological Society, the largest gathering of evangelical scholars in the world. The theme this year is &#8220;Christ in All Scripture.&#8221; This year I will be delivering the presidential address at the Thursday night banquet. The title of my lecture [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
