      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 7624,
        "date": "2019-10-14T08:40:28",
        "date_gmt": "2019-10-14T12:40:28",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=7624"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T17:58:16",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T21:58:16",
        "slug": "how-dangerous-is-money-a-great-new-resource-for-avoiding-the-pitfalls",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/how-dangerous-is-money-a-great-new-resource-for-avoiding-the-pitfalls/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "How Dangerous is Money? A Great New Resource for Avoiding the Pitfalls"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>Ok, so we all know the main Bible verse about money: &#8220;The love of money is a root of all sorts of evil&#8221; (1 Tim 6:10).  In fact, we know it so well that we rarely let it sink in.<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"7627\" data-permalink=\"https://michaeljkruger.com/how-dangerous-is-money-a-great-new-resource-for-avoiding-the-pitfalls/newheiser-money/\" data-orig-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1650,2551\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Newheiser money\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money-1024x1583.jpg\" class=\"alignright wp-image-7627\" src=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"304\" height=\"470\" srcset=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money.jpg 1650w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money-400x618.jpg 400w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money-768x1187.jpg 768w, https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/10/Newheiser-money-1024x1583.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 304px) 100vw, 304px\" /></p>\n<p>If we ponder it for just a brief moment, we would realize that money, though it can be a blessing, can also be one of the most dangerous things in the world.  If a person is not careful, it can shipwreck your life.</p>\n<p>For this reason, I am very thankful for <a href=\"https://rts.edu/people/dr-james-newheiser-jr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jim Newheiser&#8217;s</a> recent volume, <a href=\"https://amzn.to/35tByhp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>Money: Seeking God&#8217;s Wisdom</em></a> (P&amp;R, 2019).  Jim is director of the <a href=\"https://rts.edu/degree/macc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">biblical counseling program</a> here at <a href=\"https://rts.edu/campuses/charlotte/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RTS Charlotte</a> and brings deep, pastoral, biblical wisdom on this important issue.</p>\n<p>Needless to say, in the world of Christian ministry, money issues are often front-and-center in the lives of your congregation. Whether you&#8217;re a pastor or a counselor, this book will help you address those issues with compassion and grace.</p>\n<p>Another thing I love about this book is that it is in the form of a 31-day devotional.  In fact, I plan to work through this volume with my kids in our morning devotionals.  It&#8217;s a great opportunity to get them thinking about the blessings and pitfalls of money.</p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s the book description:<!--more--></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">Do you have money troubles? Often the underlying issue is not money but the promise of security, possessions, and pleasure that it brings. To lay a strong foundation for true financial success usually involves a change in perspective rather than in income. Biblical counselor Jim Newheiser&#8217;s reflection questions and practical exercises, paired with Scripture&#8217;s wisdom on financial and work-related topics, point you toward fiscal responsibility on earth and treasure in heaven.</p>\n<p>And some great endorsements:</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;A timely gift for those who seek to live biblically in a culture that is saturated with the pitfalls of materialism.&#8221; &#8212;<b>T. Dale Johnson</b>, Executive Director, Association of Certified Biblical Counselors; Associate Professor of Biblical Counseling, Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;This devotional points to solid biblical wisdom that will ground readers who feel tossed about by waves of financial woe.&#8221; &#8212;<b>Curtis Solomon</b>, Director, The Biblical Counseling Coalition</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;This wonderful book . . . provides Christians with God&#8217;s money wisdom in the most accessible format I have seen.&#8221; &#8212;<b>James C. Petty</b>, Author, <i>Act of Grace</i>; Executive Director Emeritus, Children&#8217;s Jubilee Fund</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&#8220;I would put the topic of finances within the top five issues that people whom I counsel struggle with. Here, Jim . . . [guides] us in this area of daily tension in our walk with God.&#8221; &#8212;<b>Stuart W. Scott</b>, Professor of Biblical Counseling, Graduate Program of The Master&#8217;s University</p>\n<p>You can get the book <a href=\"https://amzn.to/2q5ZpU9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>.  For more on Charlotte&#8217;s counseling program, see <a href=\"https://rts.edu/degree/macc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>.</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Ok, so we all know the main Bible verse about money: &#8220;The love of money is a root of all sorts of evil&#8221; (1 Tim 6:10).  In fact, we know it so well that we rarely let it sink in. If we ponder it for just a brief moment, we would realize that money, though [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
