          "og_description": "Over the last number of years, I&#8217;ve had the opportunity to spend a lot of time in the writings of the Apostolic Fathers.  The Apostolic Fathers are an informal collection of early Christian writings, roughly 95-150 AD, which include books like the Didache, 1 &amp; 2 Clement, the Epistle of Barnabas, and letters from Polycarp [&hellip;]",
          "og_url": "https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/were-the-earliest-christians-only-concerned-about-oral-tradition-2/",
