        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>Should We Read the Bible Critically or Confessionally? Two New Resources - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/should-we-read-the-bible-critically-or-confessionally-two-new-resources/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Should We Read the Bible Critically or Confessionally? Two New Resources - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"In the world of biblical scholarship, it has long been clear that there are two very different ways of approaching the biblical text.  And these different approaches determine whether scholars find historical (or theological) value in the words of Scripture. On the one side is the higher-critical approach. Generally speaking, this approach is marked by [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/should-we-read-the-bible-critically-or-confessionally-two-new-resources/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2019-07-10T15:22:27+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2023-04-14T21:58:25+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2018/05/judging-e1526315938336.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1000\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"469\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"tw