        "title": {
          "rendered": "Persistent Myths about the Origins of the New Testament"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>Are the NT manuscripts corrupted?  Have scribes irreparably changed the text?  Were Christian scribes competent to copy the text reliably?</p>\n<p>How many &#8220;other&#8221; gospels were there in early Christianity? Were these gospel suppressed by &#8220;orthodox&#8221; groups? Were these lost gospels as popular as the canonical ones?</p>\n<p>Don Carson and I answer these questions for a <a href=\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/podcasts/tgc-podcast/don-carson-mike-kruger-persistent-myths-new-testament/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TGC video</a>:</p>\n<p>[iframe width=&#8221;1000&#8243; height=&#8221;550&#8243; src=&#8221;https://www.youtube.com/embed/soRcOA-3pa4&#8243; frameborder=&#8221;0&#8243; allow=&#8221;accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&#8221; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>Are the NT manuscripts corrupted?  Have scribes irreparably changed the text?  Were Christian scribes competent to copy the text reliably? How many &#8220;other&#8221; gospels were there in early Christianity? Were these gospel suppressed by &#8220;orthodox&#8221; groups? Were these lost gospels as popular as the canonical ones? Don Carson and I answer these questions for a [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
