        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>Hello, My Name is God - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/hello-my-name-is-god/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Hello, My Name is God - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Did Jesus think he was God? This may be one of the most common questions people ask about early Christology. And it reflects a long-standing scholarly debate about Jesus&#8217;s own divine consciousness. Even if other people thought Jesus was divine, did Jesus himself think so? A number of years ago, Bart Ehrman jumped into the [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/hello-my-name-is-god/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2019-05-13T12:23:01+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2023-04-14T21:58:29+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2019/04/Jesus-as-God-e1556645034654.jpg\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1276\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"650\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpeg\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"5 minutes\" />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schem