      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 7146,
        "date": "2018-12-27T10:17:25",
        "date_gmt": "2018-12-27T15:17:25",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=7146"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T17:57:41",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T21:57:41",
        "slug": "rts-charlotte-womens-bible-study-has-a-new-look",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/rts-charlotte-womens-bible-study-has-a-new-look/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "RTS Charlotte Women&#8217;s Bible Study Has a New Look"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>As many of you know, from 2014 to 2016 I led a women’s Bible study on the <a href=\"http://rts.edu/charlotte/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RTS Charlotte</a> campus on the book of Romans–42 installments in all.</p>\n<p>Starting in 2017, the women&#8217;s Bible study resumed with the book of Hebrews.  This past fall, we just finished the 25th installment and plan to wrap up the book in the Spring.</p>\n<p>We continue to be encouraged to hear that the videos are being watched by folks all over the country and the world.  I even heard a recent story of someone coming to Christ by watching the videos in California.</p>\n<p>For those interested in getting the videos and handouts, RTS just launched a new website and the Hebrews study has a new look.  You can find the first 25 HD videos of Hebrews <a href=\"https://rts.edu/hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>, and we have also assembled all the study notes (thus far) into an <a href=\"https://rts.edu/hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">e-book</a> for you to download.</p>\n<p>You can also download each handout individually. You will see the <a href=\"https://rts.edu/resources/introduction-to-hebrews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">link</a> to individual handouts as soon as you click on one of the videos to watch.</p>\n<p>Due to the transition in the website, I have received a lot of emails lately asking where the videos went. Thanks for your patience as we work out the kinks.</p>\n<p>If you are looking for the Romans videos/handouts, we are still working on that.  In the meantime, you can find the Romans videos <a href=\"https://rts.edu/series/rts-charlottes-womens-bible-study-romans/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a> (handouts are not up yet).</p>\n<p>Also, please know you can always find the Romans and Hebrews videos on <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/search?q=RTS+Charlotte+women%27s+bible+study\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vimeo</a>.</p>\n<p>For those looking to get a feel for the study, here&#8217;s my welcome video for the Hebrews study as well as the first installment:<!--more--></p>\n<p><iframe title=\"RTS Charlotte: Women&#039;s Bible Study 2017 Announcement\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/222401848?dnt=1&amp;app_id=122963\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write\"></iframe></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><iframe title=\"RTS Charlotte: Women&#039;s Bible Study (Hebrews) w/ Dr. Michael Kruger; Episode 1\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/233877213?dnt=1&amp;app_id=122963\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write\"></iframe></p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>As many of you know, from 2014 to 2016 I led a women’s Bible study on the RTS Charlotte campus on the book of Romans–42 installments in all. Starting in 2017, the women&#8217;s Bible study resumed with the book of Hebrews.  This past fall, we just finished the 25th installment and plan to wrap up [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
