        "slug": "is-the-old-testament-still-relevant-for-christians",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/is-the-old-testament-still-relevant-for-christians/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Is the Old Testament Still Relevant for Christians?"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>It goes without saying that there has been a lot of chatter lately about the applicability of the Old Testament for new covenant believers.  For instance, you can check out my <a href=\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TGC</a> article, &#8220;<a href=\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/reviews/irresistible-andy-stanley/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Why We Can&#8217;t Unhitch from the Old Testament</a>,&#8221; a review of Andy Stanley&#8217;s latest book on this topic, <a href=\"https://amzn.to/2Q4LD0f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Irresistible</em></a>.</p>\n<p>But, some people don&#8217;t have time for a lengthy article, and certainly not a book.  If you (or someone you know) is looking for just a brief 3-minute summary of why the OT still matters, then here&#8217;s a video I did recently for <a href=\"https://credomag.com/2018/11/is-the-old-testament-still-relevant-today-new-credo-video-with-michael-kruger/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Credo Magazine</a> on this very question:</p>\n<p>https://vimeo.com/303131785</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>It goes without saying that there has been a lot of chatter lately about the applicability of the Old Testament for new covenant believers.  For instance, you can check out my TGC article, &#8220;Why We Can&#8217;t Unhitch from the Old Testament,&#8221; a review of Andy Stanley&#8217;s latest book on this topic, Irresistible. But, some people [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
