      "sourceMetadata": {
        "id": 6831,
        "date": "2018-06-20T08:00:01",
        "date_gmt": "2018-06-20T12:00:01",
        "guid": {
          "rendered": "http://michaeljkruger.com/?p=6831"
        },
        "modified": "2023-04-14T17:56:13",
        "modified_gmt": "2023-04-14T21:56:13",
        "slug": "interested-in-getting-a-biblical-counseling-degree-without-moving-now-you-can-do-it-rtscharlotte-2",
        "status": "publish",
        "type": "post",
        "link": "https://michaeljkruger.com/interested-in-getting-a-biblical-counseling-degree-without-moving-now-you-can-do-it-rtscharlotte-2/",
        "title": {
          "rendered": "Interested in Getting a Biblical Counseling Degree without Moving?  Now You Can Do It @RTSCharlotte"
        },
        "content": {
          "rendered": "<p>This past week, I spoke at the <a href=\"https://2018.thegospelcoalition.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TGC Women&#8217;s conference</a> in Indianapolis.  I did three sessions on a number of different topics, but the highlight was the <a href=\"https://wp.me/p2dVaB-1LF\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RTS-sponsored lunch conversation</a> where Melissa and I discussed why theology matters for women.</p>\n<p>Afterwards, I was asked repeatedly about which degree program would be helpful for women wanting to go to seminary.  Although all our programs are great, I think the RTS Charlotte <a href=\"http://rts.edu/Site/RTSNearYou/Charlotte/MACC/overview.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Master of Arts in Christian Counseling</a> degree (MACC) is a wonderful option.</p>\n<p>What makes the MACC degree distinctive is that half of the 66 credit hours are in Bible and theology.  Thus, MACC students not only know <em>how</em> to counsel, they know the crucial <em>content</em> of their counseling.</p>\n<p>And here&#8217;s the big news:  we recently <a href=\"http://www.rts.edu/charlotte/newsevents/newsdetails.aspx?id=2645\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">announced</a> that we are now offering the MACC degree in an new Summer/Winter format.  <em>This means that students can now get the MACC degree over the course of four years without having to relocate.</em></p>\n<p>Let me say that again.  You can get the MACC without moving.</p>\n<p>But, here&#8217;s the thing that makes the Charlotte program unique: <em>our counseling classes are not taken online</em>.  They are all residential classes right here in Charlotte.  They are simply done in intensive formats during the winter and summer.</p>\n<p>Given that counseling is inherently a relational exercise, we think it is a bit counter-intuitive to get a counseling degree by only plugging in the head phones and looking at a computer screen.  Instead, counseling is best taught and learned in a <a href=\"https://biblicalcounselingcoalition.org/2018/03/12/face-to-face-counseling/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">face-to-face environment</a> where students can interact with each other and with the professors.</p>\n<p>So, we are excited to see how this new Summer/Winter MACC program can allow people to get a degree without  moving, but at the same time preserving the important face-to-face, relational aspects of counseling.</p>\n<p>In addition, Charlotte&#8217;s biblical counseling degree has a number of other distinctives:<!--more--></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Committed to the gospel message and the sufficiency of God&#8217;s Word as the basis of all counseling</li>\n<li>Our program shares the same biblical perspective on the counseling task as modeled in organizations like the Christian Counseling and Educational Foundation (CCEF) and the Biblical Counseling Coalition (BCC).</li>\n<li>Phenomenal visiting faculty including Ed Welch, Rod Mays, Jeremy Pierre, Heath Lambert, Deepak Reju, and Bob Kellemen</li>\n<li>More than half the MACC curriculum is Bible and Theology, laying a critical foundation for counseling</li>\n<li>A director, <a href=\"http://rts.edu/Site/RTSNearYou/Charlotte/MACC/faculty.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jim Newheiser</a>, with over 25 years of counseling experience</li>\n<li>Located in beautiful city of Charlotte on a gorgeous 17 acre campus</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To read more about the new program, see <a href=\"http://rts.edu/Site/RTSNearYou/Charlotte/MACC/overview.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.  The formal press release is <a href=\"http://www.rts.edu/charlotte/newsevents/newsdetails.aspx?id=2645\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>Hope to see you in a counseling class soon!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
        "excerpt": {
          "rendered": "<p>This past week, I spoke at the TGC Women&#8217;s conference in Indianapolis.  I did three sessions on a number of different topics, but the highlight was the RTS-sponsored lunch conversation where Melissa and I discussed why theology matters for women. Afterwards, I was asked repeatedly about which degree program would be helpful for women wanting [&hellip;]</p>\n",
          "protected": false
        },
