        "yoast_head": "<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v28.5 - https://yoast.com/product/yoast-seo-wordpress/ -->\n<title>Did the Church Fathers View Their Own Writings as &quot;Inspired&quot; Like Scripture? - Canon Fodder</title>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" />\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Did the Church Fathers View Their Own Writings as &quot;Inspired&quot; Like Scripture? - Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"A number of years ago, Albert Sundberg wrote a well-known article arguing that the early church fathers did not see inspiration as something that was uniquely true of canonical books.[1]  Why?  Because, according to Sundberg, the early Church Fathers saw their own writings as inspired.   Ever since Sundberg, a number of scholars have repeated this [&hellip;]\" />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://michaeljkruger.5mt.site/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture/\" />\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Canon Fodder\" />\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2018-01-29T13:21:27+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2018-01-31T00:37:08+00:00\" />\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://5mt.michaeljkruger.com/2012/04/twelve2-e1483625394866.png\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"975\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"361\" />\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/png\" />\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"Michael Kruger\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"5 minutes\" />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\\/\\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture\\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture\\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"Michael Kruger\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/b985803864f1d81b09c01a0aa8aa6d22\"},\"headline\":\"Did the Church Fathers View Their Own Writings as &#8220;Inspired&#8221; Like Scripture?\",\"datePublished\":\"2018-01-29T13:21:27+00:00\",\"dateModified\":\"2018-01-31T00:37:08+00:00\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture\\/\"},\"wordCount\":1065,\"commentCount\":3,\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/#\\/schema\\/person\\/b985803864f1d81b09c01a0aa8aa6d22\"},\"image\":{\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture\\/#primaryimage\"},\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https:\\/\\/5mt.michaeljkruger.com\\/2012\\/04\\/twelve2-e1483625394866.png\",\"keywords\":[\"Apostolic Fathers\",\"Church Fathers\",\"Inspiration\",\"Lee McDonald\",\"NT Canon\"],\"articleSection\":[\"Authority of Scripture\",\"Jesus Tradition\",\"New Testament Canon\"],\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"potentialAction\":[{\"@type\":\"CommentAction\",\"name\":\"Comment\",\"target\":[\"https:\\/\\/michaeljkruger.5mt.site\\/did-the-church-fathers-view-their-own-writings-as-inspired-like-scripture\\/#respond\"]}]},{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https:\\/\\/micha